+// Camoufox: Windows legacy styled-family names (LEAKS #168).
+//
+// DirectWrite groups faces into weight/width/slope families, so on Windows
+// "Arial Black" is not a family: it is the GDI name of Arial's Black face, a
+// legacy name that stock Firefox learns only from the name tables its
+// deferred font-info loader reads (gfx.font_loader.delay is 60 s on Windows,
+// or sooner once a legacy name is asked for). Until those aliases land, its
+// lookup goes through FontList::FindFamily's XP_WIN fallback
+// (SharedFontList.cpp:1234-1316): the first time, it reads the base family's
+// face names into the per-process mAliasTable and answers with the BASE
+// family, so "Arial Black" renders as Arial Regular; every later lookup of a
+// name of that base hits mAliasTable and calls FindFamily(mBaseFamily, true)
+// with the base's display name ("Arial"), which never matches the lowercase
+// keys, so the name is missing and the next family in the list is used. On
+// stock win-i9 the fonts.detect probe sees exactly this: the first column
+// measures the base family, the next two the generic fallback.
+//
+// fontconfig has no such names: "Arial Black" is an ordinary family here, so
+// an identity claiming Windows on this host answered with the real Black face
+// every time. These are the bundle's fonts that are legacy names on Windows:
+// a static face whose typographic family (nameID 16) is its nameID 1 minus
+// the last word, plus the faces without nameID 16 that stock win-i9 measured
+// as legacy (2026-10-31): Franklin Gothic Medium and Demi, which DirectWrite's
+// family-name parsing folds into "Franklin Gothic", and Gill Sans MT Condensed
+// and Tw Cen MT Condensed (Franklin Gothic Book, also without nameID 16, is a
+// family there). The nameID 16 rule is kept for names win-i9 did not measure:
+// it picks out all 15 nameID 16 names the win-i9 probe saw act as legacy and
+// none it saw act as families. Variable fonts are left out. Sorted
+// (LC_ALL=C) for the binary search.
